body:
GA, I'm stuck and Marcus is waiting. The MCM dashboard at https://marcusash.github.io/motor-city-math/ shows zero scores despite multiple fix attempts. Need your eyes on this.

WHAT MARCUS SEES: Empty dashboard. No chart data. No score percentages. "YOUR PROGRESS" section shows legend but no chart. "Up Next" shows generic "Retake Practice" instead of specific RP number. Same result after clearing browser cache and hard refresh.

WHAT I'VE TRIED (all deployed and verified on live site):
1. Added async auto-seed: if localStorage empty, fetch data/kai-scores-latest.json and populate. Result: no change.
2. Created dad.html redirect page for ?dad=1 URL param. Result: Marcus not using it, and ?dad=1 mode also fails.
3. Inlined score data directly in HTML as synchronous script. Runs before main script. Sets localStorage from inline JSON if empty. VERIFIED this code is on live site. Result: STILL no scores showing.

VERIFIED WORKING:
- data/kai-scores-latest.json exists and returns valid JSON (I fetched it remotely)
- index.html on live site contains inline score seed script (I fetched the HTML and confirmed)
- GitHub Pages build completed for commit c9709e5

THE INLINE SEED CODE (at top of body):
(function() {
    try {
        var existing = localStorage.getItem('mcm_scores');
        if (existing && existing !== '{}' && existing !== 'null') return;
    } catch(e) {}
    var _serverScores = {full score JSON here};
    try { localStorage.setItem('mcm_scores', JSON.stringify(_serverScores)); } catch(e) {}
})();

HYPOTHESES I CANNOT VERIFY FROM HERE:
1. localStorage might be blocked by Edge enterprise policy on Marcus's machine
2. A JS error in an earlier script (chart.min.js, chart-theme.js) might halt execution before inline seed runs. But seed is in body, those are in head.
3. The inline seed might work but rerenderAll() might be throwing silently before it can render charts
4. Browser might be serving an aggressively cached version despite Ctrl+Shift+R

WHAT I NEED FROM YOU:
1. Open the site in your browser (or any test browser) and check if scores appear
2. Open browser DevTools console and check for JS errors
3. In console, run: JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('mcm_scores')) and see if data is there
4. If data IS in localStorage but chart is empty, the bug is in buildChart() or rerenderAll()
5. If data is NOT in localStorage, the seed script is being blocked somehow

The score data (4 tests: original 53%, RP1 87%, RP2 87%, RP3 100%) should show in the progress chart and in the All Tests section.

This is blocking Marcus right now. Please investigate ASAP.
